# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Patient-level clinical data  --  MUST NOT be published
#
# These patterns are deliberately broad and are written without relying on
# case-insensitive matching, because git's `core.ignorecase` is true on macOS
# (APFS) but false on Linux: a pattern that appears to work locally can start
# tracking files on a collaborator's or CI machine.
#
# See PATIENT_DATA_AUDIT.md for the full inventory of what these cover.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Raw clinical trial source data (per-patient tumour measurements, cell dose,
# IL-2 doses, CISH-KO assay results, for every enrolled subject)
CISH_pt_data.xlsx
cish_pt_doses.xlsx

# HPC job logs: these echo per-patient filenames, subject IDs and fitted
# values as the fits run. They are build output, never source.
julia_output_*.txt
julia_error_*.txt
slurm-*.out

# Simulated-therapy results (inputs to Fig 7). Rows are keyed by tumour
# ("patient_002_tumor_1") and hold fitted parameters plus simulated outcomes.
# The two clinical columns (initial_tumor_size, cish_dose) have been removed
# from the tracked copies -- nothing reads them -- so what remains is entirely
# model-derived and Fig 7 reproduces from a clean clone. Unmodified originals
# are in _archive/original_parameter_tables/.

# Per-patient longitudinal CISH-KO ratio measurements (UMN IDs in content)
CISHKO_Pct_result.csv

# Per-patient uncertainty and prediction outputs
optimal_parameters_by_patient.csv
Uncertainty_AllPatients.csv
real_patient_predictions.csv

# Anything carrying a subject identifier in its name: per-patient fit figures,
# per-patient likelihood profiles, per-patient schedule trajectories
*UMN_0*
*UMN0*
Patient_*
patient_*
Profile_Likelihood_*
Aggregate_Profile_*

# ...except the model-derived parameter tables, which ARE published as Table D
# in S1 Text. Shipping them lets Figs 4-8 be reproduced from a clean clone with
# no access to the clinical data. The two clinical columns (initial_tumor_size,
# cish_dose) have been removed from the tracked copies of the *_with_ratio table;
# unmodified originals are kept in _archive/original_parameter_tables/.
# These re-include rules must stay AFTER the broad patterns above.
!Patient_UMN_*_paras.json
!patient_tumor_params.csv
!patient_tumor_params_with_ratio.csv

# Manuscript supplement source: captions/labels enumerate the full subject
# roster (UMN_002-UMN_022). Un-ignore only after de-identifying the captions.
supplement_figures.tex

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Superseded / scratch material kept on disk but not published
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
_archive/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local output directories
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
output/
outputs/
results/
tmp/
figures/generated/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch, logs, editor and OS cruft
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.asv
*.zip
*.jl.cov
*.jl.mem
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
.julia/

# Note: Project.toml and Manifest.toml are intentionally NOT ignored --
# both are committed so that Pkg.instantiate() reproduces the exact
# environment used for the manuscript.
